Subject: [PATCH] Dispersion re-fit conditioned on FP historical projections
 (2020-2025)

--projections mode for fit_allocation.py: NB/gamma likelihoods conditioned
on FantasyPros projected means (via ff_playerids crosswalk, 30,078 joined
player-weeks) instead of EW history -- matching how the live sim conditions.

Head-to-head vs empirical spread within FP projection bands: FP-conditioned
std within 0.1-0.4 pts of empirical at every position; the EW fit ran wide
because EW mean error leaked into dispersion. Count k values rise across the
board (QB cmp_k 18->29, RB att_k 4.1->7.4, WR tgt_k 11->17); TD counts are
~Poisson given a calibrated projected mean (k at the 400 bound for QB/RB/WR)
-- the EW fit's TD overdispersion was mean error, not real spread.

Share precisions (weekly_phi) and feature priors remain EW-based; FP does
not project team shares.

Known remaining miss, deliberate: simulated floors are slightly high vs
empirical (fatter real-world left tail from blowouts/early exits). That is
shared game-environment variance -- item 14's hierarchical sim, not
per-player dispersion.

